# Shared rules

- SPEC.md is the source of truth. Implement only the phase you are asked to implement.
- Python 3.11+, uv, full type hints, mypy --strict on src/, ruff format and ruff check.
- Write tests first wherever SPEC.md gives expected outputs.
- No network access in tests; LLMs and external APIs are stubbed.
- Never log or commit secrets. Never commit real personal data.
- Record significant decisions and spike outcomes as ADRs in docs/adr/ using the template there.
- If SPEC.md is ambiguous, stop and list the ambiguity; do not invent behaviour.

# Project rules (from SPEC.md, Appendix A)

- Only synthetic data. Never add real identifiers to code, tests, or docs, except a publicly listed GSTIN used solely to verify the check-char algorithm.
- Generated datasets stay under data/generated/ and are git-ignored.
- The base library (bharat_pii.detect, bharat_pii.validate) must not import heavy optional dependencies.
